  "solution": {
    "approach": "Compute product of all numbers from 1 to n (factorial of n).",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) == 1) {\n        long long fact = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) fact *= i;\n        printf(\"%lld\\n\", fact);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (cin >> n) {\n        long long fact = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) fact *= i;\n        cout << fact << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int n = sc.nextInt();\n            long fact = 1;\n            for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) fact *= i;\n            System.out.println(fact);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys, math\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        print(math.factorial(int(s)))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\n    if (s.length > 0) {\n        const n = parseInt(s, 10);\n        let fact = 1n;\n        for (let i = 1n; i <= BigInt(n); i++) fact *= i;\n        console.log(fact.toString());\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Iterate from 1 to n and multiply into a cumulative product variable initialized to 1."
  },
